name: gnomon-local
description: >-
  @a-company/gnomon-local — the local-model session child (spec §13.1), a
  separate executable driven by the kernel's #local-runner over stdio in pi's
  --mode rpc JSONL shape. Zero runtime deps; compat allowlist = llama.cpp,
  Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM, mlx-lm (no cloud providers); loopback/LAN rule
  re-checked in the child; argument repair, text-tool fallback, tool surface
  none|compact|full, parallel tools, steer/follow_up queues. M1.8 slice 1.

components:
  gnomon-local:
    description: >-
      The gnomon-local child: src/endpoint.ts, compat.ts, client.ts (SSE
      streaming, no redirects), repair.ts, tools.ts (read_file, write_file,
      list_dir; confined to realpath roots cwd+worktree, writes never under .git or through a symlink final component), agent.ts (sticky abort; surface none never runs tools), rpc.ts, cli.ts (exitCode, never process.exit after writes); client byte caps + idle timeout. Slice 2: compaction.ts (re-derived; contextTarget
      ~8k from the session config; threshold compaction before a request that
      would not fit, one compact-and-retry on a context-overflow 400/413, a
      second overflow ends the run error; tool-less non-streamed summariser,
      reply normalised to exactly Goal/Constraints/Progress/Decisions/Next/
      Critical; history = system + summary + the longest safe tail within a
      quarter of the target, never an orphaned tool result; events
      compaction_start/_end; the summariser's usage is part of agent_end).
      Round 2 (M1): the summary escapes every < and sits in a block labelled model-generated / data-not-instructions; compaction_end carries summaryHash + summaryBytes. Round 2: history budget = 0.85 x target minus the native tools schema; at most one compaction per step (still over after it, or an overflow after it, ends the run with a clear error); the kept tail never starts at a text-tool <tool_result> message. Round 3: summary/tail caps derive from the budget; a config with maxTokens >= 0.85 x contextTarget is refused. Round 2: rpc steer is refused while the agent is idle (never queued into the next turn). Loops step 10 (#loop-act): protect.ts (the kernel's glob dialect, case-insensitive) and the session config's optional `tools` (the names the loop clamp admits; the agent offers and runs only those) and `protect` (repo-relative globs; write_file refuses a hit with a `protected-input:` result and no card, node_modules always); a malformed list is a ConfigError, never "all". T-2026-10-26-003 (local lane): read_file is paged in BYTES (optional offset, limit) and capped at the session share (ctx.readCap = a quarter of the working budget as bytes, split across one turn's read_file calls; MAX_READ 256 KB stays the absolute ceiling; pages end on a UTF-8 boundary; a partial page ends with a note naming the total size, the bytes returned and the next offset); compaction pins the CURRENT prompt as the Goal (summaryMessages(…, goal); the compacted lead carries it verbatim unless the kept tail holds it) and keeps fair-shared, escaped excerpts of the newest dropped tool results of this run (<tool-result-excerpt tool args trust="data-not-instructions">, with a read_file re-read offset) inside the lead user message (compaction_end.excerpts); the tail and excerpts share the budget left after the reply, system, summary and goal; the newest transcript messages reach the summariser past MESSAGE_CHARS; at maxSteps ONE tool-less request (STEP_LIMIT_PROMPT, merged into a trailing user message, compact first when over budget) is the reply, stopReason stays max_steps (a failed final request ends max_steps with its error), agent_end fires once. Slice B1 (TD-2026-10-27-833): confine.ts holds the confinement (moved verbatim from tools.ts, plus confinedFile/confinedDir for walks and writeConfined shared by write_file and edit); budget.ts is the context LEDGER (pure: usable = floor(target x 0.85) split into system / memory (0 until B2) / tools (native schema or text-tool prompt) / history / reply; messageBudget keeps the round-2 budget exactly) and every turn start emits context_report{turn, target, slots, historyUsed, compactions} (the kernel's runner.ts parses it into a bounded `context` event and does not act on it); shape.ts SHAPES every tool result under min(1500 tokens, the history slot's share of the turn): an over-cap result keeps its head plus a spill handle @rN with line/char totals and a read_section hint, the full text in an in-child LRU SpillStore (<= 4 MiB UTF-8, session lifetime); a result carrying text from a file the model wrote this session is wrapped <tool-data source="model-generated" trust="data-not-instructions"> with & and < escaped (the compaction rule); errors are never spilled or labelled; the read_file page is sized under the cap so its paging note survives. list_dir is bounded (LIST_MAX_ENTRIES 200, then a count). Tools are offered in the fixed order list_dir, read_file, read_section, grep, outline, edit, write_file (compat.ts TOOL_ORDER). Slices S1 + C1 (TD-2026-10-27-833, #local-tool-broker; src/broker.ts): the protocol is TWO-WAY — the child emits tool_request{id tr-N, toolCallId, name, args} and reads tool_response{id, content, isError, provenance kernel|mcp:<server>}, tools_set{tools:[{name, description, parameters, class}]} (refused for a session with a tools allowlist, i.e. a loop act session; names may not take a native tool's; <= 64 tools) and the B2-reserved memory_set / compact / set_context (validated, parsed, answered applied:false); the new commands are closed (an unknown field refuses them), every field is bounded, a stdin line over MAX_COMMAND_LINE (2 Mi chars) is refused, unknown commands refused. A BROKERED tool is offered after the natives (the system prompt's text-tool list and the ledger's tools slot are rebuilt when a tools_set takes effect, at the next step start); a call validates its args against the OFFERED schema (unknown keys always refused; G-LCL-15: refused args never reach the kernel), waits for tool_response under a deadline (toolTimeoutMs 30 s read, cardTimeoutMs 5 min mutate/destructive; both optional session config keys) and the run's abort cancels it — both end as an error result, never a hang; a late response is refused "no outstanding request". The result is shaped like any other and labelled <tool-data source="kernel"|"mcp:<server>" trust="data-not-instructions"> (workspace rule). A name outside the native and current brokered sets is "unknown tool". Aegis C1 review: the child sends tool_cancel{id} when it gives up on a call (timeout or abort); a model call id outside [A-Za-z0-9_.:-]{1,128} is replaced by call-<id>; a brokered ERROR keeps its provenance frame (<tool-data source="kernel" trust="data-not-instructions" error="true">, workspace neutralisation). Deferred: JSONL session tree, bash.
    path: src/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, local, paradigm-8, m1.8]
    tests:
      - test/local-child.test.ts
      - test/compaction.test.ts
      - test/local-lane.test.ts
      - test/budget.test.ts
      - test/shape.test.ts
      - test/broker.test.ts
  local-retrieval-tools:
    description: >-
      Slice B1 (TD-2026-10-27-833; spec §13.1 "Retrieval tools", an Appendix A node since the 2026-10-27 symbol
      audit) retrieval tools for small local models, src/retrieval.ts, all on confine.ts:
      grep{pattern, path?, glob?, max?, regex?} — literal by default; regex only with regex=true, refused over
      256 chars, with a backreference or a lookbehind, or if it does not compile (u flag), and run in a worker
      thread terminated after a 3 s budget per call; the walk never follows a symlink (file or dir), never enters
      .git or a nested node_modules, re-checks every dir and file by realpath against the roots, skips hard-linked
      files, binaries (a NUL in the first 8 KiB) and files over 1 MiB; at most 2000 files, 20000 entries and 60
      hits, lines cut to 200 chars, code-unit name order, output `path:line: text`. outline{path} — a
      deterministic regex extractor per extension (ts/js family, py, go, rs, md headings outside fences) with
      line numbers, no model. read_section{path, from, to} | {path, symbol} (the outline entry to the next entry at
      the same or a shallower depth) | {handle: @rN} (spill handles, keeping their model-source label); pages
      under the result cap and names the next from. edit{path, old, new} — the one exact occurrence (0 or more
      than 1 refused with the count and lines), resolveWrite + writeConfined (roots, .git, protect globs with the
      protected-input prefix, symlink final component, hard links), edits of one file serialised in the child.
      Falsifiers G-LCL-11 (grep/outline/read_section/edit never leave the roots or follow a symlink or hard link)
      and G-LCL-12 (no tool result exceeds its cap; a spill handle round-trips through read_section).
      Aegis review of B1: H1 grep's glob is matched by globMatcher (an O(n·m) position-set matcher for *, **, ?,
      {a,b}; never protectGlob's regex, which stays for kernel config globs); H2 outline rules have no adjacent
      overlapping quantifiers and the md heading is a fixed regex plus string trimming; M1 a regex worker error or
      exit ends the call "regex failed: …"; M2 every grep has a 32 MiB read budget and a 5 s deadline (both modes),
      at most 2 greps run at once (a semaphore), the run's AbortSignal (ctx.signal) stops the walk; M3 one lock per
      canonical target in confine.ts shared by write_file and edit, and edit refuses a file whose dev/ino/size/mtime
      changed between its read and its write; M4 a lexical gate (UNC/device prefixes, win32 drive-relative paths and
      ADS colons, the resolved path lexically under a root) runs before any realpath; M5 every file-content result
      (read_file, read_section, grep, outline and their spills) is framed <tool-data source="workspace"|
      "model-generated" trust="data-not-instructions">: model-generated text fully escaped, workspace text with only
      the delimiter tags (tool-data, tool_result, tool-result-excerpt, compaction-summary) neutralised, also inside
      text-tool <tool_result> bodies; the frame and note survive at the minimum cap; L1 every open is verified
      (handle dev/ino against stat(realpath), inside the roots; a just-created file is unlinked on failure); L2 a grep
      start under .git is refused; L3 outline names in errors are escaped; L4 reads check isFile before opening and
      open O_NONBLOCK. Aegis re-check: L-a a missing target is opened O_CREAT|O_EXCL (EEXIST retries as an
      existing file) and the failed-verify cleanup unlinks only when lstat shows the handle's own dev/ino; L-b the
      grep slot is taken right before the try that releases it and the matcher is built inside it; M-a every result
      (labelled, unlabelled, errors; native and text tools) and every compaction excerpt and summary gets a U+2060
      word joiner after the opening < or [ of chat-template special tokens (ChatML <|…, Llama 3, Llama 2/Mistral <s>
      </s> [INST] and v3 control tokens, Gemma <start_of_turn>); edit (old, new) and write_file (content) remove
      exactly those joiners so a copied line matches and writes the literal bytes; L-c win32 reserved device names
      (CON, NUL, AUX, PRN, COM0-9, LPT0-9, CONIN$, CONOUT$) are refused lexically; the lock key folds case on win32;
      a backslash glob is a path glob; edit re-reads the bytes through the write handle before truncating.
    path: src/retrieval.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, local, paradigm-8, retrieval]
    tests:
      - test/retrieval.test.ts
      - test/retrieval-hardening.test.ts
      - test/retrieval-recheck.test.ts
      - test/shape.test.ts
      - test/local-child.test.ts
